@startuml
!theme plain
title TASK-260715-30zng6 — M1 startup, rollback and idempotent stop
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Provider callback" as NE
participant "TunnelProviderAdapter\nactor" as Adapter
participant "RuntimeCoordinator\nactor" as C
participant "Config source" as Config
participant "SSH bootstrap" as SSH
participant "TCP + DNS" as Consumers
participant "Packet plane" as Plane
participant "Settings builder/applier" as Settings
participant "Snapshot store" as Snap

== Ordered start ==
NE -> Adapter: start(configuration envelope v1)
Adapter -> Adapter: require idle; generation += 1
Adapter -> C: make generation + structured cancellation root
C -> Snap: starting/configuration; all capabilities false
C -> Config: decode, bounded atomic load, validate references
Config --> C: immutable non-secret snapshot
C -> C: require production M0 binding permit for production root
C -> SSH: resolve/connect on physical path
SSH -> SSH: evaluate host evidence before credential/auth
SSH --> C: verified session + actual remote endpoint
C -> Consumers: prepare TCP flow consumer
Consumers --> C: TCP prepared
C -> Consumers: prepare DNS with SSH-only TCP upstream
Consumers --> C: DNS ready
C -> Plane: pure preflight(bound M0 packet/HEV configuration)
Plane --> C: validated; no descriptor/HEV/listener/read acquired
C -> Settings: build compatible plan(actual endpoint, DNS, MTU)
Settings --> C: validated plan
C -> Settings: apply(plan, generation)
Settings --> C: committed
C -> Plane: activateReads(generation) / existing PacketBridge.start
Plane --> C: private ingress + read + mandatory supervision live
C -> C: re-check SSH/TCP/DNS/packet health
C -> Snap: usableTCPDNS; TCP + safeDNS true; UDP false
C --> Adapter: start success
Adapter --> NE: complete exactly once

== Partial-start failure ==
alt failure before settings apply
  Config -[#red]> C: or SSH/consumer/plane error
  C -> Snap: stopping; capabilities false
  C -> C: reverse acquired-resource stack
  C -> Plane: reset preflight or stop/join only if activation raced
  C -> Consumers: stop/join acquired consumers
  C -> SSH: idempotent close if acquired
  C -> Snap: failed; routesInstalled=false
  C --> Adapter: stable primary error + cleanup summary
else failure/cancel after settings commit
  Plane -[#red]> C: activation or final health failure
  C -> Snap: stopping; capabilities false
  C -> Plane: stop reads / bridge / HEV and join
  C -> Settings: clear(generation)
  alt clear confirmed
    Settings --> C: cleared
  else clear failed or uncertain
    Settings -[#red]-> C: stable clear safety error
    C -> Snap: failed; routesInstalled=true; routeState=clearFailed
  end
  C -> Consumers: stop DNS then TCP
  C -> SSH: idempotent close
  C -> Snap: failed; route fields match clear result
  C --> Adapter: stop returns Void after snapshot/log publication
end

== Stop or mandatory runtime failure ==
NE -> Adapter: stop(reason)
Adapter -> C: stop(reason)
C -> C: create or join one shielded cleanup task
C -> Snap: stopping; capabilities false; close admission
C -> Plane: stop reads / bridge / HEV and join
opt settings committed or commit outcome uncertain
  C -> Settings: clear and await; retain truthful failure/uncertainty
end
C -> Consumers: stop DNS transactions, then TCP flows
C -> SSH: close channels/session/socket
C -> Snap: disconnected if clear not required/confirmed;\nfailed + clearFailed only when required clear failed/uncertain
C --> Adapter: stop returns Void
Adapter --> NE: complete exactly once

par repeated/concurrent stop
  NE -> Adapter: stop(reason)
  Adapter -> C: stop(reason)
  C -> C: join existing cleanup task
  C --> Adapter: same nonthrowing completion
else stale callback
  Settings -[#gray]>> C: old generation completion/event
  C -> C: discard; state/routes/snapshot unchanged
end
@enduml
